{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2171-03-07 00:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good evening. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the surgery team doctors. You're here because of left upper quadrant pain. Can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2171-03-07 00:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started about two days ago. It’s near my g-tube site. I usually tolerate my feeds, but today I just don’t feel like eating because of the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2171-03-07 00:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any nausea, vomiting, fever, or changes in bowel movements?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2171-03-07 00:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever or chills. I haven’t had diarrhea or constipation. Just the pain and not wanting to eat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2171-03-07 00:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Given your history of Roux-en-Y bypass and the g-tube in your gastric pouch, we need to check if the tube is in the right place. We’ll get some labs and likely replace the tube tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2171-03-07 00:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Replace it? I thought it was working fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2171-03-07 00:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The imaging team wants to confirm the position. Sometimes these tubes can shift. We’ll do it under imaging guidance to make sure it’s placed correctly in the pouch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2171-03-07 00:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2171-03-07 00:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get mild sedation—fentanyl and Versed—so you’ll be relaxed. Local numbing at the site too. Most patients tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2171-03-07 00:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2171-03-07 06:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs came back. White count is slightly up but not concerning. Kidney and liver tests are normal. We’re still planning the tube replacement today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2171-03-07 06:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any sign of infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2171-03-07 06:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No fever or clear infection signs. The tenderness near the tube might be from irritation or granulation tissue. We’ll check that during the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2171-03-07 06:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. They used silver nitrate last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2171-03-07 06:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. If it’s there, we’ll treat it again. Helps reduce discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2171-03-07 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to start the procedure. You’ll feel some pressure, but let us know if it’s painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2171-03-07 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2171-03-07 15:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Procedure is done. We successfully replaced the tube in your gastric pouch. The old one had shifted slightly. We also treated some granulation tissue with silver nitrate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2171-03-07 15:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the new tube secure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2171-03-07 15:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s secured with a Flexi-Trak and the site is dressed. You should feel better soon. Pain is already improving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2171-03-07 15:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, less pressure now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2171-03-07 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your evening labs look stable. Hemoglobin is steady, white count came down a bit. Good signs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2171-03-07 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Can I start drinking anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2171-03-07 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with small sips. You’re tolerating oral intake so far, which is great. We’ll advance slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2171-03-07 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my regular meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2171-03-07 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve restarted your home meds: pantoprazole, sucralfate, nortriptyline, and the others. We’re increasing nortriptyline to 100 mg at night for better pain control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2171-03-07 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that helped last time. What about the tube feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2171-03-07 17:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We discussed that. Since the pouch connects to your esophagus, feeding through the tube might not be effective. We’re not restarting feeds for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2171-03-07 17:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why keep the tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2171-03-07 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You chose to keep it for now. We can revisit removal later. It’s there if needed, but not required for feeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2171-03-07 17:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. Pain is controlled with oral meds, you’re walking, and tolerating food. We’re planning discharge today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Any restrictions at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the tube site clean and dry. Wash with soapy water daily. No baths or swimming. Watch for redness, swelling, or fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if the pain gets worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use the oxycodone elixir as needed, every 4 to 6 hours. But call us if pain doesn’t improve in 24 hours, or if it spreads to your chest or back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll see your surgeon soon for an endoscopy to check your anatomy. Also, continue all your vitamins and iron."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re adding a lidocaine patch near the tube site for comfort. And temazepam for sleep if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You can go home later this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate all the help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if anything changes or concerns you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2171-03-08 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2171-03-07 00:29:00",
    "admission_end": "2171-03-08 19:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for left upper quadrant abdominal pain near her gastrostomy tube site. She has a history of Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and cyclic vomiting syndrome requiring a gastrostomy tube for nutritional support. She underwent fluoroscopy-guided replacement of the gastrostomy tube due to malposition and granulation tissue at the site, which was treated with silver nitrate. Post-procedure, her pain improved, and she tolerated oral intake. The decision was made not to restart tube feeds due to anatomical concerns. She was restarted on home medications with an increase in nortriptyline to 100 mg nightly for pain management and discharged home with instructions for tube site care, pain control, and follow-up endoscopy.",
    "problems": [
      "Abdominal pain, left upper quadrant",
      "Persistent vomiting",
      "Unspecified protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Bariatric surgery status"
    ]
  }
}
